version 2.0.0 (prerelease — TODO)
===============================
BREAKING: unified forecast format. Consolidate GFS and ERA5 readers into a
single Forecast class operating on CF-compliant ECMWF-style netCDF. Archived
v1 forecasts will require one-time conversion.

Phased plan (strangler-fig, evaluation suite as safety net):

* Phase 0: Safety net is the unit test suite
    * `tests/` (945 tests) covers analytical truth for 10 scenarios across
      both readers, cross-reader equality, smoke tests, and the 2 real
      forecast files pinned in config_earth. Every phase must keep it green
    * (Internal-only) flight-data eval baseline is not part of this repo;
      run it privately at each phase against your own archived flights as
      an additional check beyond the unit tests

* Phase 1: Define canonical schema
    * Write `docs/forecast-schema-v2.md`: CF-1.7, ECMWF-style. Variables `u,
      v, t, z`; dims `time/level/latitude/longitude`; lat descending; level
      ascending hPa; time as CF "hours since"; geopotential `z` in m²/s²
    * Verify existing ERA5 archived files already conform (likely a no-op
      semantically — if eval drifts here, a hidden dependency on
      non-canonical detail has been found)

* Phase 2: Update ERA5.py to read the canonical format directly
    * Current ERA5.py reads the v1 "processed" format (dims `time`, `level`
      ascending hPa, `z` already pre-divided by g) — output of the now-
      obsolete `convert_era52gfs.py`. The raw Copernicus CDS downloads
      (e.g., `BASS_ERA5_20210721_20210722.nc`) are ALREADY in the v2
      canonical format and currently require the "-processed" intermediate
    * Rewrite ERA5.py to consume v2 directly: read dims `valid_time` /
      `pressure_level` / `latitude` / `longitude`; drop the `[::-1]` level
      flip (canonical `pressure_level` is descending hPa → altitude is
      already ascending with index); keep the `z / g` geopotential→meters
      conversion (canonical `z` is m²/s²)
    * Delete `forecast_processing/convert_era52gfs.py` and the
      `*-processed.nc` artifacts; archived raw `BASS_ERA5_*.nc` files load
      through the updated reader as-is
    * Pre-Sep-2024 ERA5 archives (e.g., `SHAB14V_ERA5_20220822_20220823.nc`,
      CF-1.6, dims in reverse order) are handled later by `migrate_v1`
    * Verify the unit test suite still passes; both real-forecast tests in
      `test_real_forecasts.py` now need the BASS file (v2-format) as their
      reference

* Phase 3: Make saveNETCDF.py write canonical
    * Update the GFS downloader to emit canonical-format files directly:
      rename vars `ugrdprs/vgrdprs/hgtprs/tmpprs` → `u/v/z/t`; rename dims
      `time/lev/lat/lon` → `valid_time/pressure_level/latitude/longitude`;
      convert `hgtprs` (meters) → `z` (m²/s²) by multiplying by g; convert
      longitude from `[0, 360)` to `[-180, 180)`; flip latitude to
      descending; re-encode time as `seconds since 1970-01-01` with
      `calendar="proleptic_gregorian"`; add `Conventions = "CF-1.7"`
    * GFS-downloaded canonical files become readable by the v2 ERA5.py

* Phase 4: Migrate archived v1 forecasts
    * Add `python -m EarthSHAB.forecast_processing.migrate_v1 <file_or_dir>`
      CLI: detects v1 GFS-style (`ugrdprs` vars), v1 ERA5 "processed"
      (`time`/`level` dims), and pre-Sep-2024 ERA5 (CF-1.6 with reversed
      dim order); converts each to v2 canonical in place; backs up original
      as `<name>.v1.nc`. Idempotent
    * Add ForecastFormatError raised by the reader when a v1 file is
      detected, with the exact migration CLI in the message
    * Add `docs/migration-v2.md`: what changed, how to detect v1 files,
      how to convert, why no auto-conversion (explicit > silent data mutation)

* Phase 5: Collapse the readers
    * Rename `ERA5.py` → `Forecast.py` (it's the canonical reader now)
    * Delete `GFS.py`, `forecast_processing/convert_gfs2era5.py`
      (`convert_era52gfs.py` already deleted in Phase 2)
    * Update `config_earth.forecast['forecast_type']` semantics — single
      forecast type, source distinguished by file provenance metadata

* Phase 6: Test suite cleanup
    * Drop `reader_type` parametrization from `tests/conftest.py` — single
      reader, ~half the test count (~470 instead of 945)
    * Delete `tests/tools/reader_adapter.py` (no schema mismatches left to
      normalize)
    * Simplify `tests/tools/make_dummy_forecasts.py` to emit only canonical
      schema; delete `_write_gfs_style` and the GFS time pre-shift hack

* Phase 7: Documentation + release
    * README banner: v2.0 breaking change + link to migration doc
    * Final eval pass against the Phase 0 baseline — must match within
      existing cross-method tolerance for every flight
    * Net diff target: ~-800 lines

Sequencing: each phase a separate commit (preferably PR). If eval drifts
between phases, the cause is localized to the latest phase.

Latent bugs in v1 surfaced by the test suite (worth fixing during this
refactor since the offending code is being deleted):
* ERA5.py:167 — unpacks 3 values from a 2D `np.nonzero`; only fires on
  partial mask at the level-0 sample slice
* GFS.py:70 — hardcoded `"days since 0001-01-01"` units with
  `has_year_zero=True` produce cftime objects and a 2-day calendar offset
  vs stdlib datetime


version 1.3.1
===============================
* Added evaluation support for Helium Augmented and GrandSlam flights (ignoring ascent phase in evaluation)
* Added new wind interpolation methods, selectable via `config_earth.forecast['wind_interpolation']`
* Added batch comparison script `python -m evaluation.compare_batches <A> <B>`
* Fixed blank GFS hodograph in `plot_windmap` - `plotWind2` was indexing the full netCDF arrays with cropped-region indices, landing in the wrong geographic cell


version 1.3 
===============================
* Fixed bug in calculating sunset off of sim trajectory for ground-truth data
* Sunset tracking added to model and trajectory plots
* Evaluation Suite against Historical Data
    * Recreating https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/atot/41/12/JTECH-D-24-0045.1.xml?tab_body=pdf
    * Single-flight evaluator: `python -m evaluation.evaluate`
        * Forward simulation + reforecast (forecast winds applied to truth altitude profile) with plots
        * Phase detection (ascent / float / descent)
    * Batch evaluator: `python -m evaluation.run_batch --note "..."`
    * Multi-format APRS loader (aprs.fi standard, raw onboard logger, LightAPRS-W variants)

version 1.2.1
===============================
* Reorganizing into Python package Structure
* Make main more modular
    * simulate.py added, and individual plotting scripts added to Plotting/


version 1.2.0
===============================
* New saveNETCDF.py script with discontinuation of NOAA's OpenDAP Server
    * Also works with AWS GFS Script (slightly different results due to formatting/conversion)
* Now supports Python==3.11 and many newer dependencies
* Added some intial forecast processing test cases between GFS sources
* Added Edge Case Handling for GFS boundary loopups to match ERA5 behavior
* Note: GFS download from NOAA vs AWS has slight differences


version 1.1.0
===============================
* Added ERA5 reanalysis functionality
* Added Documentation in readthedocs format
* Updated the netcdf lookup scheme in GFS to be significantly faster
* Added checks to see if simulation will go out of bounds or over time
* Configuration file reorganization and update


version 1.0.1
===============================
* Added predict.py and rainbow trajectory prediction for multiple float altitudes

version 1.0.0
===============================
* The original EarthSHAB software
